**Product Requirements Document (PRD)**  

---

### 1. Waveform Animation  
**User Story**  
As a user of Claude Dictate, I want the audio waveform to animate in real‑time while I speak, so I can see visual feedback that my voice is being captured.  

**Acceptance Criteria**  
- The waveform updates continuously during voice input without lag.  
- Animation starts when recording begins and stops when recording ends.  
- No visual artifacts or freezes occur on supported platforms (Windows 10+, macOS 12+).  

**Technical Constraints**  
- Must use the existing rendering pipeline; no third‑party graphics library may be added.  
- Animation must run at ≥30 fps on default hardware configurations.  

---

### 2. Settings Persistence  
**User Story**  
As a user, I want my selected model and other settings to be saved automatically so that they remain unchanged after I close and reopen the application.  

**Acceptance Criteria**  
- Selected model persists across application launches.  
- All configurable settings (e.g., language, output format) are stored in a user‑specific configuration file or registry entry.  
- On first launch, defaults are applied; on subsequent launches, saved values are loaded.  

**Technical Constraints**  
- Persistence must be implemented using the existing JSON‑based settings file located in the user data directory.  
- No sensitive data may be stored in plain text.  

---

### 3. UI Loading & Inference Animations  
#### 3.1 Model Loading Animation  
**User Story**  
When a model is being loaded, I need a clear visual cue and explanatory text so I understand the system is busy.  Realtime summary of the terminal output including character/token count should be displayed.

**Acceptance Criteria**  
- An animated spinner appears centered in the model selection area.  
- Text “Loading model…” is displayed beneath the spinner.  
- Animation remains until the model is fully loaded or an error occurs.  

#### 3.2 Inference Progress Animation  
**User Story**  
During LLM inference, I want feedback that processing is ongoing, preventing the impression that the app has frozen.  

**Acceptance Criteria**  
- A progress animation (e.g., pulsing bars) is shown in the response pane.  
- Accompanying text “Generating response…” is displayed.  
- Animation stops when the response is rendered or an error is returned.  

#### 3.3 “Refine with LLM” Step Animation  
**User Story**  
When I trigger the “Refine with LLM” action, I need an animation that confirms the refinement process has started.  

**Acceptance Criteria**  
- A distinct animation (e.g., rotating gear) appears next to the “Refine with LLM” button.  
- Text “Refining output…” is shown.  
- Animation ends when refinement completes or fails.  

**Technical Constraints (All UI Animations)**  
- Animations must be built with the existing React‑Native animation framework; no external animation libraries are permitted.  
- All animations must be accessible (ARIA‑compatible) and respect reduced‑motion system settings.  

---

### 4. Prompt Format Support for Claude Code  
**User Story**  
As a developer, I need the system to generate prompts in Claude Code’s preferred format so that downstream refinement works without manual conversion.  

**Acceptance Criteria**  
- The application detects when Claude Code is the target LLM.  
- Prompts are automatically formatted according to Claude Code specifications (e.g., markdown code fences, specific token delimiters).  
- Existing refinement styles remain unchanged for other LLMs.  

**Technical Constraints**  
- Prompt formatting logic must be added to the existing `PromptFormatter` module.  
- No changes to the core inference API contract.  

---

### 5. Output Directory Browser Visibility  
**User Story**  
When I launch Claude Dictate, I want the output directory browser to be visible immediately, ensuring all essential UI functions are accessible without extra clicks.  

**Acceptance Criteria**  
- The output directory selector panel is displayed on the main screen at startup.  
- If the panel was previously hidden, it reappears automatically on launch.  
- The layout adapts gracefully on different screen sizes (minimum width 1024 px).  

**Technical Constraints**  
- UI layout must use the existing Flexbox grid; no redesign of the overall window architecture.  
- Visibility state should be stored using the same settings persistence mechanism described in Section 2.  

---

### 6. General Usability Enhancements  
**User Story**  
As a frequent user, I expect a smooth, responsive interface with consistent visual feedback throughout all interactions.  

**Acceptance Criteria**  
- All new animations and UI elements are tested for performance impact; CPU usage must not exceed 15 % on baseline hardware during idle animation.  
- Accessibility audits (WCAG 2.1 AA) pass for all added components.  
- Regression testing confirms no loss of existing functionality.  

**Technical Constraints**  
- All code changes must maintain compatibility with the current Electron 22 runtime.  
- No increase in application bundle size greater than 5 MB.

